<Plain title="Privacy Policy" description="What data Secure Mac App collects: analytics (with consent), the beta waitlist email list, your GDPR rights and how to ask us to delete your data." path="/privacy/" updated="27 Oct 2026">
  <p>We collect as little as we can. This page explains what runs on the site and what we do with it.</p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> measures which pages are read and which buttons are clicked. It starts with analytics storage denied (Consent Mode v2) and only stores analytics cookies if you click Accept in the cookie banner.</li>
    <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> records anonymised sessions and heatmaps. It loads only after you accept, and form inputs are masked.</li>
    <li>Your choice is stored in your browser (<code>localStorage</code>) along with your theme preference. No advertising cookies are used.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Email list</h2>
  <p>If you join the Secure Vault waitlist we store your email address, the page you signed up from, your language, and any campaign tags in the URL, with our email provider (Buttondown). We use double opt-in: you must confirm by clicking a link. We email you when the beta opens, and send Mac privacy tips only if you ticked that box. Every email has an unsubscribe link.</p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on Vercel, which keeps standard server logs (IP address, user agent, requested URL) for security and operations.</p>

  <h2>Your rights (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to access, correct or delete the data we hold about you, to restrict or object to processing, and to export it. Email <a href="mailto:hello@securemacapp.com">hello@securemacapp.com</a> and we will respond within 30 days. You can also complain to your local data-protection authority.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we will update the date above.</p>
</Plain>
